From ad8107da4724980fc0a7bbc618cdcccf912f9eb0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 17:41:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] Replace human-approval gate with automated PPTX
 knowledge-deck pipeline

Milestone 2 now runs unattended end-to-end (query -> auto-decide -> publish
-> generate/upload knowledge PPTX) per the updated Yoxa workflow, so the
approve/revise/reject UI and its backend are dead weight. This wires the
codebase up to match:

- Remove the HITL webhook route, approval-response route, approval API
  client, and approval card component (all unreferenced now).
- Add /api/webhooks/yoxa-pptx to receive the new "Generate and Upload
  Vendor Knowledge PPTX" Output Tool delivery and persist it via a new
  save-vendor-knowledge-document edge function (already deployed) into the
  new vendor_knowledge_documents table + vendor-knowledge-pptx storage
  bucket (already migrated in Supabase).
- Add vendor-knowledge.ts client + pollForKnowledgeDocument poll helper.
- Rewrite /vendor/solution-dna as a read-only status screen: shows live
  capability verification status while the agent works, then surfaces a
  "Your Vendor Knowledge Deck is ready" card with a download link once the
  PPTX lands. No approve/reject actions remain.
